Subject: [PATCH 3/8] vm: virtual entry-boundary rerouting for bytecode targets
 (no trampoline)

Two base-engine changes (both NON-version-hash, iOS-viable, base-resident) that
let an UNCHANGED base-AOT instance call reach a runtime-transplanted bytecode
method:

1. aot_call_specializer.cc TryReplaceWithDispatchTableCall: env-gated
   SANKOFA_NO_TABLE_DISPATCH keeps instance calls switchable (IC) instead of
   baked dispatch-table calls, so the site can re-resolve to a transplanted
   target.
2. runtime_entry.cc DoICDataMissAOT: skip the monomorphic-direct-call transition
   for target_function.HasBytecode(). The monomorphic path enters
   MonomorphicEntryPoint with R0=receiver and never loads FUNCTION_REG; the
   InterpretCall stub needs FUNCTION_REG=Function. The polymorphic
   ICCallThroughCode/MegamorphicCall stubs DO load FUNCTION_REG (R0 on arm64),
   so keeping bytecode targets there routes them to the interpreter correctly.

Proven on host (override_in_place probe 3): with SANKOFA_NO_TABLE_DISPATCH=1 base
build, transplanting only Widget.build flips renderNew() (render UNCHANGED) from
'render-> BASE-UI' to 'render-> PATCH-UI-FIXED'. No per-function trampoline, no
runtime codegen. Sync to sankofa-dart-sdk fork.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runtime/vm/compiler/aot/aot_call_specializer.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 runtime/vm/runtime_entry.cc                     | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/aot_call_specializer.cc b/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/aot_call_specializer.cc
index 6f3f550905e..94e6f67de66 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/aot_call_specializer.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/aot_call_specializer.cc
@@ -1183,6 +1183,20 @@ const Function& AotCallSpecializer::InterfaceTargetForTableDispatch(
 
 void AotCallSpecializer::TryReplaceWithDispatchTableCall(
     InstanceCallBaseInstr* call) {
+  // [sankofa] Optionally keep instance calls as switchable IC calls instead of
+  // baked dispatch-table calls. A dispatch-table call jumps to a flat uword[]
+  // entry baked at snapshot time, so it cannot reach a function whose body was
+  // replaced by a runtime bytecode transplant. A switchable IC call re-resolves
+  // through the IC/megamorphic miss handler, whose stubs (MegamorphicCall,
+  // ICCallThroughCode) load FUNCTION_REG before entering the target — exactly
+  // what the InterpretCall stub needs — so a transplanted (bytecode) target is
+  // reached correctly. This is the virtual entry-boundary mechanism: build the
+  // base app with SANKOFA_NO_TABLE_DISPATCH=1 so framework -> your build() stays
